Subject: Continue processing zip readers with rejected member names

Origin: DHI-internal (Go 1.26 compatibility)
Description: Treat zip.ErrInsecurePath as a per-member warning because SanitizeZipMemberName independently rejects non-local names before opening archive members.
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/seaweedfs/seaweedfs.git b65832bdc9bbbcf3682465b1be598627ac386206
Verify: cmd `go test ./weed/server -run '^TestExtractZipArchivePut$'` expect "ok"
Forwarded: no (the 4.49 release and current upstream branch still reject the complete archive under Go 1.26)
Drop-When: upstream >= 4.50 (once extractZipArchive handles zip.ErrInsecurePath)

Go 1.26 enables archive path validation by default and returns a usable zip reader together with zip.ErrInsecurePath. Continuing with that reader lets the existing sanitizer reject only unsafe members while preserving valid files from the same archive.

--- a/weed/server/filer_server_handlers_extract.go
+++ b/weed/server/filer_server_handlers_extract.go
@@ -74,2 +74,2 @@ func (fs *FilerServer) extractZipArchive(ctx context.Context, w http.ResponseWri
-	zr, err := zip.NewReader(ra, size)
-	if err != nil {
+	zr, err := zip.NewReader(ra, size)
+	if err != nil && !errors.Is(err, zip.ErrInsecurePath) {
